<BaseLayout title="Clearance overview | UXO.INFO" description="An overview of professional explosive ordnance clearance.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Professional remediation</p><h1>Clearance is specialist work.</h1><p class="lead">The work of reducing explosive risk is planned and evidence-led. It is not something an individual should attempt from general internet guidance.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container split"><div><h2>From information to safer access.</h2></div><ol class="numbered"><li><span>01</span><div><h3>Understand the context</h3><p>Professionals gather relevant records, local knowledge, and evidence to understand where a hazard may be present.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3>Assess and prioritize</h3><p>Work is planned around risk, people, land use, and applicable standards—not just what is visible at the surface.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3>Clear, document, and hand back</h3><p>Qualified teams investigate and address hazards within defined procedures, record the work, and support safe use of land where appropriate.</p></div></li></ol></div></section>
<section class="section section--quiet"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Important boundary</p><h2>Do not handle suspected ordnance.</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>If you encounter a suspected explosive item, do not touch or move it. Keep others away where this can be done safely and contact the relevant local emergency, police, military, or explosive-ordnance authority.</p><p>UXO.INFO is not an emergency reporting channel.</p></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
